    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0313" n="306" xml:id="pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-31T11:00:00+08:00">July 31, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 31—6:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. Department’s 115, July 13, 2 p.m.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d323-f1"/> and my
                    247, July 16, 6 p.m. from Peiping. In a conversation which I had with British
                    and French Ambassadors yesterday it appeared that communication made to French
                    Foreign Office by Japanese Ambassador in Paris was not made to British Foreign
                    Office by Japanese Ambassador there. Can Department inform me whether Japanese
                    Ambassador in Washington gave any assurances regarding South China or made any
                    statement as to Japanese intentions in regard to North China?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
